## Project Structure

```
src/
├── core/           # Pure logic, no I/O
│   └── ...         # Business logic, validation, models
│
└── shell/          # I/O adapters
    └── ...         # CLI, API, file operations
```

**Key rule:** Core imports are one-way. Shell imports from Core, never the reverse.

---

## Quick Rules

1. **Separation:** `src/core/` (pure) vs `src/shell/` (I/O)
2. **Contracts:** `@pre`/`@post` for Core functions
3. **Results:** `Result[T, E]` for Shell functions that can fail
4. **Verify:** Run `invar guard` + `pytest` after changes

---

## Development Workflow

Follow **ICIDV** for each task:

### I - Intent
```
□ Understand what needs to be done
□ Identify affected files
□ Classify as Core or Shell
```

### C - Contract
```
□ Define function signature with types
□ Add @pre/@post decorators
□ Write doctest examples
```

### I - Inspect
```
□ Check target file size (if >200 lines, be careful)
□ Check existing function signature patterns
□ Identify edge cases
```

### D - Design
```
□ If file will exceed 280 lines → plan extraction
□ Match existing signature patterns
□ Plan integration tests if adding config options
```

### I - Implementation
```
□ Write code (< 50 lines per function)
□ Keep files < 500 lines
□ No **kwargs or eval in Core
```

### V - Verify
```
□ pytest --doctest-modules (unit)
□ invar guard (architecture)
□ Test config scenarios (integration)
```

---

## Verification Commands

```bash
# Run all tests including doctests
pytest --doctest-modules

# Check architecture rules
invar guard

# Check only modified files (shows INSPECT info)
invar guard --changed

# Detailed explanations for violations
invar guard --explain
```

